-- #1111 A-2.5 SEVERITY-LADDER MIRROR — the `exit 1 must STAY exit 1` half.
--
-- A-2.5's user-visible win is that a valid program stops being rejected
-- (`1092_method_scope_named_b`'s sibling in test/llvm_fixtures_modules/
-- method_scope_valid_under_collision, an `exit 1 → exit 0` change).  The failure
-- mode of getting that wrong is that impl obligations stop being RECORDED at all,
-- which turns every missing impl into silence — a strictly worse S0 than the one
-- being fixed, and one that NO drained repro can see, because every drained repro
-- contains a name collision and this file contains none.
--
-- So: one interface, one method name, no collision anywhere in the graph, and no
-- `impl MOnly Blob`.  `check` must report exactly one error:
--
--   No impl of MOnly for Blob; write an 'impl MOnly Blob'.
--
-- This is the path A-2.5 leaves entirely alone (the method table's collided-name
-- list is EMPTY here, so `applyMethodScopeOverrides` returns the floor map
-- untouched) — which is exactly why it is worth pinning: "the overlay is a no-op
-- when nothing collides" is an assertion, not an observation, until something
-- grades it.
import mone.{MOnly, solo}

public export data Blob = Blob

main = println (solo Blob)
